From 031c96cd1f131151f5294c3ac51450d13cb1a285 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pengdonglin <pengdonglin@xiaomi.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:59:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dump: preserve captured DWARF names for matching scalar
 arguments

Save user parameter names and ABI locations in backward-compatible .dbg
comments while recording, including explicit -A specifications without
automatic argument capture. Resolve the correct session, module and symbol
once per exported call, then emit nullable names aligned with user_args.

Require matching argument locations rather than assuming source parameter
order, preserve captured widths and bytes, and decline conflicting names,
malformed metadata, specialized compiler clones and broken type layouts.
Offline export continues to work after the original ELF and source vanish.

Add native tests for ABI matching, width changes, per-symbol isolation,
conflicts, CRLF and rejected malformed or overflowing metadata. Verify
115 native unit tests pass with one existing skip, plus 103 project
argument-name, export, caller, import, detail and fullscreen regressions.
---
